        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/takewalker/{size}/5677_2.png",
        "created_at": "2019-10-01T16:03:34.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>First, to answer their question, I had been looking at the incap side of SaD Benchmark's (non?)foil character card, the one that had a bunch of villains, and so I thought Count Barzakh was Baron Blade under a different name. This also led me to believe \"barzakh\" meant \"knife\"? And that it was spelled \"barzoc\". :B So we can chalk it all up to me being not very bright.</p>\n<p>Second, some Amazon links to the book series Christopher was talking about:&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Perdido-Street-Station/dp/B002BU5R4G/ref=pd_sbs_129_1/130-0214598-4393475?_encoding=UTF8&amp;pd_rd_i=B002BU5R4G&amp;pd_rd_r=484d674a-857f-4e6d-aa44-7754244e195a&amp;pd_rd_w=GJyew&amp;pd_rd_wg=UkzLt&amp;pf_rd_p=d66372fe-68a6-48a3-90ec-41d7f64212be&amp;pf_rd_r=FZKHPJRK6VT84GGW9YST&amp;psc=1&amp;refRID=FZKHPJRK6VT84GGW9YST\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">Perdido Street Station</a>,&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Scar-New-Crobuzon-Book/dp/B00OZYTWG0/ref=sr_1_2?keywords=the+scar&amp;qid=1569945291&amp;s=books&amp;sr=1-2\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">The Scar</a>. I'll definitely check those out one day.</p>\n<p>Third, I was of course mentally constructing a villain deck for Count Barzakh while listening to the episode, because that's something I do, but I got a little discouraged when I realized all I had come up with was basically the Cauldron's Swarm Eater. :B</p>\n<p>And last but not least, my favorite part of this episode was when I said \"...to move you\" at the exact same time as Christopher. XD Validation!</p>",
